  "body": "The proposed QQ16 A/T shear separates an earlier witness but does not recover every required input. This contribution supplies a complete counterexample for that restoration obligation and proves a broader obstruction to selected-only boundary controls. No new \u03ba.\n\nTwo executions with different original selected inputs remain indistinguishable to the permitted observations. This holds for arbitrary deterministic selected-only interventions beginning after the complete F0, including affine, nonlinear, adaptive, cross-bank and cross-owner controls with initially identical auxiliary state. The local F/B maps and ordinary event schedule remain fixed.\n\nExact result:\n- The credited three-port witness uses ordinary ports 2, 8 and 85, with chart axes 37, 38 and 506.\n- B_s h = 0 for every s = 1,...,8, while B0 h(I) = (2,2,0,0,0,0,2,-2).\n- The original X_A difference at identity owner is (-1,0,-1,-1,0,1,0,0).\n- All selected observations, five forward histories and completed-X descendants agree through the retained 19-event schedule.\n- The remaining difference is in the former-Y endpoint, outside the permitted observation contract.\n\nThe written two-execution induction establishes the quantified claim. Finite fixtures are regressions, not a proof by sampling. Granting every added operation and implementation cost free still leaves restoration impossible, so no valid improved recurrence is claimed.\n\nNovelty and predecessor credit:\n- Ali Romman's PR1969 supplies the conserved QQ16 maps, native packet and retained schedule.\n- Adam Gall's PR2093 supplies the three-port common-kernel witness. Its discovery is not claimed here. This contribution extends its implication to pre-B1 selected-only interventions and arbitrary equal-state controls.\n- Cinna Davis's PR2216 supplies the specific shear and its separately scoped old-witness separation result. This result does not contradict that local claim.\n- Adam Gall's PR2086 provides the adjacent changed-A-logger obstruction.\n- @commdata2338's PR2174 supplies the adjacent two-query recovery contract and the warning about actual F2/F8 pair binding.\n- Retained supplier and compiler attribution remains in the unchanged source notices.\n\nExact provenance:\n- Starting main: 0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2\n- Priority revision: 4; OS assignment seed: 58, recursive interfaces.\n- PR2093: 8b21a900eb520e4f11ea177b310f66316f8e8983\n- PR2216: b80e9ba43367fb8b20877a97da1cb677c34f9264\n- PR2174: f79470a7931f3943360c10d15b428e0e4e479c22\n- QQ16 packet SHA256: a5ed85fac5ebf3c091482a113ab0d351eb5a7892fe2841a35e16017ec1ff49f7\n- Retained archive SHA256: 22c3f4dce4b897a1d423d1388801933e288b6a6b1906cb15e1b16a5eb68db754\n\nAll consumed files have Git-blob/SHA256 pins in SOURCES.json. Pending predecessor executables are neither imported nor vendored.\n\nReproduce from the repository root, using Python 3.12 and the standard library:\n\n    python3 -I -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/qq16-selected-intervention-seed58\n\nExpected result:\n- PASS_QQ16_SELECTED_INTERVENTION_OBSTRUCTION\n- PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/qq16-selected-intervention-seed58 outcome=negative-result\n\nValidation actually executed on CPython 3.12.14:\n- Registered normal and optimized replays passed.\n- 1008 route bindings, 19 events and four paired-execution fixtures passed.\n- Nine controls rejected changed coefficients/axes, missing cancellation, incorrect schedule binding, forbidden ordinary access, endpoint mislabelling, a detecting B0 read and source corruption.\n- Six focused tests passed, including factored/literal backward-map agreement, nonlinear inverse/dirty-state checks and optimized CLI source/receipt mutation rejection.\n- Selected-record integrity and git diff whitespace checks passed.\n\nLimitations:\nThe result excludes only the stated observation/controller class. Ordinary reads, changed local maps, earlier input-dependent retention and changed ordinary schedules remain open. The native kernels, physical costs, precision, all-size admission and full supplier cold replay were not reverified. No proof-assistant, independent human review or hosted-CI result is claimed.\n\nUpstream main and the relevant predecessor heads were refreshed unchanged before publication. Overlap checks used local repository records, targeted public pages and Git refs; complete live pagination was unavailable. The claim and completion were recorded locally.\n\nPrepared for @CubeJerry with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in derivation, implementation, verification and writing. New material is Apache-2.0; predecessor notices and selected-frontier artifacts remain unchanged.",
